.TH WM-CAMERA 1
.SH NAME
camera \- show the camera, live
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/camera
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Camera
shows the feed at
.B /mnt/video/0
in a window, mounting
.IR camsrv (4)
there if nothing is. Holding the feed open keeps the camera on: hidden by the window
manager, or closed, it lets go, and when nothing else is reading the
camera goes off. Shown again, it takes the feed back, at the size
.B fmt
then gives: a feed turned meanwhile is shown turned.
.PP
How the camera is mounted is not the window's to say: the feed comes
the right way up from whoever started
.IR camsrv (4)
\(em its
.BR -r ,
or on a bare-metal board the card's
.B camera
file.
.PP
What is drawn over the picture is the feed's
.B layer
directory as the window's name space has it
.RI ( layers (2)):
.B bind -a
puts a layer on top,
.B bind -b
underneath, and
.B unmount
takes it off, while the window is up:
.IP
.B bind -a /mnt/vision/1/layer /mnt/video/0/layer
.PP
The camera's feed names no frames, so only a layer's
.B frame=*
records are drawn.
.PP
The keys
.B +
and
.B -
move the lens's focus,
.B a
runs autofocus once, and
.B q
exits.
.PP
With no camera, or when the camera goes, the window stays and says why;
.B q
closes it.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/camera.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR camsrv (4),
.IR layers (2),
.IR visionfs (4)
.SH BUGS
Resizing the window does not scale the picture, which stays in the
middle of it.
